# The walk cache this directory's harnesses write, not source.
#
# `r-cause-a-counterfactual.ts` appends one JSON line per parsed file to
# `cause-a-walk-<corpus-set-sha-prefix>.jsonl` and skips files already recorded, so a run
# killed by the shared 120-second parse watchdog (`src/ast/engine.ts` `process.exit()`)
# resumes instead of losing the walk. The bytes are a cache of production `parseFile`
# output over a corpus that is itself reproducible, so they are not committed. Delete the
# file, or set BB_R_FRESH=1, to force a re-walk.
cause-a-walk-*.jsonl

# Same arrangement for `r-incoming-population.ts`: one JSON line per parsed file, keyed by
# BOTH the corpus-set digest and the analyzer digest, so a spool written by one analyzer
# build can never be read as another build's result. `r-population-drift.ts` consumes these
# to name the edge separating two builds, which is why they are worth keeping on disk while
# a bisect runs, and why they are still not source.
r-incoming-walk-*.jsonl
